      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:94mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2023-june/q08-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 3. Shaded region between a parabola and a line.\"></figure><p>Figure 3 shows a sketch of a curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> and a straight line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span>.</p><p>Given that</p><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = f(x)\"></span> where <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"f(x)\"></span> is a quadratic expression in <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span></li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> cuts the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis at 0 and 6</li></ul><ul><li><span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l\"></span> cuts the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y\"></span>-axis at 60 and intersects <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span> at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"(10, 80)\"></span></li></ul><p>use inequalities to define the region <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"R\"></span> shown shaded in Figure 3.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
