      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2023-june/q10",
      "question": "<figure class=\"practice-figure\" style=\"max-width:82mm;margin:2mm auto\"><img src=\"resources/exams/edexcel-8ma0-01-2023-june/q10-figure.svg\" alt=\"Figure 4. Perpendicular lines through A, B and C.\"></figure><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = \\frac{3}{5}x + 6\"></span></p><p>The line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> is perpendicular to <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and passes through the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"B(8,0)\"></span>, as shown in the sketch in Figure 4.</p><p>(a) Show that an equation for line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> is</p><div class=\"equation\" data-math=\"5x + 3y = 40\" data-display=\"true\"></div><p><span class=\"marks\">(3)</span></p><p>Given that</p><ul><li>lines <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_2\"></span> intersect at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C\"></span></li></ul><ul><li>line <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"l_1\"></span> crosses the <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x\"></span>-axis at the point <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"A\"></span></li></ul><p>(b) find the exact area of triangle <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"ABC\"></span>, giving your answer as a fully simplified fraction in the form <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"\\frac{p}{q}\"></span></p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
