      "id": "exam/edexcel-8ma0-01-2023-june/q15",
      "question": "<p>In this question you must show detailed reasoning.</p><p>Solutions relying on calculator technology are not acceptable.</p><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = 8 - 10x + 6x^2 - x^3\"></span></p><p>The curve <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span> has equation <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"y = x^2 - 12x + 14\"></span></p><p>(a) Verify that when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = 1\"></span> the curves <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_1\"></span> and <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"C_2\"></span> intersect.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(2)</span></p><p>The curves also intersect when <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"x = k\"></span>.</p><p>Given that <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k &lt; 0\"></span></p><p>(b) use algebra to find the exact value of <span class=\"inline-math\" data-math=\"k\"></span>.</p><p><span class=\"marks\">(5)</span></p>",
